    "body": "Thank you for this report and the screenshot.\n\nTriage: `P7`, `effort:medium`. A label that is cut off with \"...\" while the panel has room is a layout defect. The values stay correct, so it is polish, not a safety problem. Related work: #2014 (a property grid with the labels on the left) and #1688 (a Geometry row label that is cut off at the default window size).\n\nIf you can, please tell us your screen resolution and the Windows display scale (for example 125 % or 150 %). Text width can change with the scale.\n",
